@startuml
skinparam lifelineStrategy solid
autonumber
title Diagrama Devoluciones 12: GET /api/v1/refunds/:id/history (Historial completo de la nota)

actor "Analista / Auditor" as User
participant "App Web" as Web
participant "Gateway Controller" as Gateway
participant "Refund History Service" as Service
participant "refund_workflow_instances DB" as InstanceDB
participant "refund_workflow_actions DB" as ActionsDB
participant "refund_workflow_instance_levels DB" as LevelsDB
participant "refund_order_detail_decisions DB" as DecisionsDB
participant "refund_orders DB" as OrdersDB

User -> Web: Abre la pestaña "Historial"
Web -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/refunds/1001/history
Gateway -> Service: getRefundOrderHistory(refundOrderId: 1001, actor)

Service -> InstanceDB: 1. findInstancesByOrder(1001)
note right of InstanceDB
  ORDER BY attempt ASC.
  Un intento por fila: el historial se lee
  por intento, no en un único hilo plano.
end note
InstanceDB --> Service: instances[] (id, attempt, status,\nreactivated_from_instance_id, started_at, finished_at)

Service -> ActionsDB: 2. findActionsByInstances(instanceIds)
note right of ActionsDB
  SELECT a.created_at, a.action, a.actor_employee_code,
         a.actor_role_code, a.comment, a.reason,
         a.system_summary, a.previous_status, a.new_status,
         a.amount_before, a.amount_after,
         a.related_refund_order_id
  ORDER BY a.created_at, a.id
  (el DDL tiene 'at' comentado: el orden
  sale de created_at)
end note
ActionsDB --> Service: actions[]

Service -> LevelsDB: 3. findLevelsByInstances(instanceIds)
note right of LevelsDB
  Da el nombre del escritorio de cada acción:
  LEFT JOIN por workflow_instance_level_id,
  que es NULL en CREATED, DISSOCIATED_CREATED,
  REACTIVATE, SELLER_RESUBMITTED, CANCEL.
end note
LevelsDB --> Service: levels[]

Service -> DecisionsDB: 4. findDecisionsByActions(itemSelectionActionIds)
note right of DecisionsDB
  Cuelga de la acción LEVEL1_ITEM_SELECTION:
  qué línea quedó SELECTED y cuál DISSOCIATED.
end note
DecisionsDB --> Service: decisions[]

Service -> OrdersDB: 5. findBridgedOrders(relatedRefundOrderIds)
note right of OrdersDB
  Resuelve la fila puente en los dos sentidos:
  - "de esta nota salió la 1004"
  - "¿de dónde salió la 1004?" ->
    WHERE related_refund_order_id = 1004
    AND action = 'DISSOCIATED_CREATED'
end note
OrdersDB --> Service: bridgedOrders[]

Service -> Service: 6. buildTimeline(instances, actions, levels, decisions, bridged)
note right of Service
  Agrupa por intento y arma la frase visible:
  system_summary (autogenerado) + comment
  (del revisor) + reason (obligatorio en
  REJECT, REACTIVATE y CANCEL).
  Las acciones con amount_before/amount_after
  muestran el movimiento del monto.
end note

Service --> Gateway: refundHistoryResponse (attempts[] con actions[])
Gateway --> Web: 200 OK
Web --> User: Renderiza la línea de tiempo por intento
@enduml
